---
import CtrCurve from "@/charts/ctr-curve.astro";
import RankRadar from "@/illustrations/rank-radar.astro";
import SectionHeader from "@/components/section-header.astro";
---

<section class="section" id="question" aria-labelledby="question-title">
  <div class="column stack" data-reveal>
    <SectionHeader id="question-title" number="1" title="Question" />
    <blockquote class="question__quote">
      Which existing pages are earning far fewer clicks than their position and their own site
      predict, beyond what bad luck explains, and will that shortfall still be there next month?
    </blockquote>
    <RankRadar />
    <p>
      Every month a content editor has thousands of live pages and time to review a few dozen. A
      page that ranks well but is not clicked is a cheap opportunity: the visibility is already
      earned. But a page can also miss clicks by chance for a month and recover on its own.
    </p>
    <p>
      A common rule flags any page in the top 20 with a click rate below 0.5%. On this portfolio the
      normal click rate sits between 0.24% and 0.42% at every position, so the rule flags most
      pages, including the ones clicking exactly as expected.
    </p>
    <CtrCurve
      title="The flat 0.5% rule flags 74% to 88% of pages at every position"
      subtitle="Share of pages with 500+ impressions that the rule flags, by average position"
      caption="Fig. 1. Even at position 2, where pages click best (0.42%), three in four pages fail the flag. The rule cannot tell a healthy page from a broken one."
    />
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .question__quote {
    padding-block: var(--space-1);
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-5);
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-statement);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--accent-ink);
  }
</style>
